<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Louis Stevenson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1850–1894</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Louis Stevenson was a Scottish novelist, author of Treasure Island and Strange Case of Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde. From 1888 he travelled in the Pacific and wrote about the Gilbertese king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tem-binoka">Tem Binoka</a> of Abemama. He settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vailima">Vailima</a> in Samoa, where he criticised German, British and American interference in A Footnote to History, and he died there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-louis-stevenson.jpg" alt="Robert Louis Stevenson" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Henry Walter Barnett · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_Louis_Stevenson_by_Henry_Walter_Barnett_bw.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
